# .npmrc — local + Vercel install behavior overrides for this repo.
#
# `legacy-peer-deps=true` was added to unblock PR #92 (eslint 9→10) on 2026-07-30.
#
# Why:
#   `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y@6.x` declares `peerDependencies.eslint = "^3 || ^4 || ^5
#   || ^6 || ^7 || ^8 || ^9"`.  Both the project's direct devDep `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y@^6.10.2`
#   and the transitive install via `eslint-config-next@16.2.12` carry that
#   range, so npm's strict peer-dep check refuses to install eslint@10.
#   Vercel's `npm install` exits 1 → `Deployment Summary: ERROR`.
#
# Trade-off (read this before removing this line):
#   This flag is project-wide and silent.  It suppresses ALL peer-dep
#   mismatches for every install (local dev, CI, Vercel) — a real
#   breaking-change peer mismatch would slip through and only manifest
#   at runtime.  Always read `npm install` output carefully on PRs;
#   peer warnings are still printed (only the failure is silenced).
#
# Remove this line when the upstream constraint clears, signalled by
# either:
#   (a) `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y@7.x` ships with `peerDependencies.eslint = "^10"`
#       (currently 6.10.x is the latest line, no 7.x yet), OR
#   (b) `eslint-config-next` bumps its transitive `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y`
#       pin to a version whose peer matches eslint@^10 (currently 16.2.12,
#       the latest line, still pins ^6.10.0).
#   Tracking issue + reversal checklist are referenced in the PR body
#   that introduced this file; `git blame .npmrc` surfaces it.
#

legacy-peer-deps=true
